// Build-A-Player College Football: generated by the CFB data build (ESPN feeds pulled 2026-11-07).
// Do not hand-edit counts; re-run the build. Assets: scripts/fetch-cfb-assets.mjs.
//
// ── Who is here ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Every 2026 FBS team: QB1 + QB2, WR1-WR3, RB1-RB2, read from ESPN's 2026 box scores (every completed game through
// Week 10). QB1 is the current starter (2026 attempts weighted toward the latest games), so a starter who is hurt
// shows as QB2 behind the man playing now (Ohio State: Fahey QB1, Sayin QB2). When only one QB has thrown a 2026 pass,
// QB2 is the ESPN-roster QB with the most college attempts; a team with no such QB has no QB2.
// QB check 2026-11-08 against each team's latest ESPN box score (Week 11 included; QB1 = the QB who took the first
//   snap): added AJ Swann (MSST QB1; Kamario Taylor out for season, dropped), Kemper Hodges (AFA QB1; Fisher dropped),
//   Mikey Keene (ASU QB2, the hurt starter, over benched Boley), Christopher Vizzina (CLEM QB2, healthy again, over
//   Pearman). QB1/QB2 swapped where the backup started the latest game: NWU, WIS, UCF, WAKE, BOIS, USU, SJSU, RICE, TEM,
//   ODU, USAL, USM, TROY, NMSU, AKR. Swapped rows keep their grades and Week 10 stat lines.
// Bio (number, height, weight, class, position) and photo: ESPN. espn = the ESPN athlete id.
// year: ESPN's class, with RS- added when ESPN's game logs show a redshirt season (no stats, or 4 games or fewer,
//   in a season since he enrolled). Approximate: ESPN has no redshirt field, and JUCO years are invisible to it.
//   Class check 2026-11-10 (scripts/cfb/class-audit.mjs, report in scripts/cfb/class-audit-report.txt): the class itself is
//   ESPN's current roster class (FR/SO/JR/SR) with the RS- flag kept, so an ESPN senior with a redshirt year is RS-SR
//   (Trinidad Chambliss). 442 of 966 rows changed, mostly RS- rows the first build had listed a class or two low.
// s26 / s25: the player's 2026 (to date) and 2025 FBS lines from ESPN's stats.
//
// ── Grade scale (the NFL 0-11 scale, read against college players) ──────────────────────────────────────────
//   0 F · 1 D · 2 C- · 3 C · 4 C+ · 5 B- · 6 B · 7 B+ · 8 A- · 9 A · 10 A+ · 11 S
//   Graded within college, so the best college players read as stars: the top 10 at a position are mostly
//   A- to A+ in what they do best, a Heisman contender is A to A+, and S is earned only by a generational few.
//   A typical Power 4 starter averages B to B+; Group of 6 starters B- to B; backups C+ to B-.
//   Checked on the output (average trait grade, size included):
//     P4 starters QB 6.7 / WR 6.8 / RB 6.3 · G6 starters QB 5.9 / WR 5.8 / RB 5.5 · backups QB 5.0 / WR 5.2 / RB 5.4
//
// ── How a grade is made ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 1. Stats: 2026 to date (weight 1.0 per attempt/catch/carry), 2025 (0.6) and 2024 (0.35), FBS games, from ESPN's stats feeds.
// 2. Each stat becomes a z-score against every graded player at the position with real volume
//    (QB 100+ attempts, WR 20+ catches, RB 40+ carries, weighted as above).
// 3. A trait is a weighted mix of those z-scores (below), re-standardized so every trait has the same spread.
// 4. Schedule: + 0.25 x the z-score of the average FPI defensive efficiency of the 2026 opponents he played (FCS = 12).
//    This is what puts an SEC or Big Ten line above the same line in the MAC.
// 5. Small samples shrink toward a prior by role: grade = n/(n+k) x evidence + k/(n+k) x prior
//    (k = 110 attempts / 22 catches / 55 carries; prior z: QB1 -0.3, QB2 -1.1; WR1 -0.1, WR2 -0.5, WR3 -0.8; RB1 -0.1, RB2 -0.6).
// 6. grade = 5.7 (+0.5 for QB) + 1.05 x slope x z (x 0.85 below average) + 0.6 x max(0, z - 1)^2
//    (slope QB 2.3, WR 1.95, RB 2.05), rounded, 0-11; 11 (S) needs z >= 2.7. One curve per position: it only
//    shifts and stretches, so no player passes another in any trait (OVR order can move a little, because Size
//    is physical and stays off the curve).
//    One named override, owner-approved: Darian Mensah (MIA) Post-Snap S (2026: 25 TD, 1 INT, Total QBR 92.9).
//    QB grades hand-checked against scouting reports, PFF grades quoted in articles and draft boards on 2026-11-07,
//    then lifted +1 in Pre-Snap, Post-Snap, Playmaking, Accuracy and Pocket for every QB (capped at A+; median QB1 OVR 81).
//    RB: 41 backs hand-graded on 2026-11-07 (every trait but Size) from PFF 2026 grades and missed-tackle counts quoted in
//    articles, preseason scouting (ESPN, PFF, The Ringer), 2027 draft boards, midseason All-America teams, verified GPS
//    speeds and recruiting; RB carrying for everyone is ball security only (see the recipe below). Round 2: every RB on
//    PFF's 2026 team grade pages (99 teams) checked; off-level ones moved toward their PFF offense grade with the stat
//    profile kept (level = 7.0 + 0.14 x (PFF - 80), G6 -0.5), plus 26 more hand rows. Ole Miss: Lacy RB2 (dislocated
//    shoulder), Makhi Frazier RB1. Miami: Fletcher RB1 (more snaps and carries than Mallory).
//    Round 3 (2026-11-08): RB1/RB2 re-checked on every team against ESPN box scores through Week 10 (carries, last three
//    games) and PFF snaps; 12 backs added (hand-graded: Ahmad Hardy, LJ Martin, Michael Barrow, the Navy slotback ESPN
//    lists as a WR, and 9 RB2s) and 16 depth orders swapped; the round-2 PFF rule run on the 28 G6 teams it had missed.
//    WR: 103 receivers hand-graded on 2026-11-07 (every trait but Size) from PFF's 2026 Weeks 1-9 yards per route run and
//    targeted passer rating for 157 Power 4 WRs, drop rates and contested catches quoted by PFF/PFN, 2027 draft boards
//    (PFF, PFN, WalterFootball, A to Z, SI), the AP midseason All-America team, verified track times and 247 recruiting;
//    the formula's routes/release/hands all ran on target share, so those were separated by role and drops. 46 flat
//    small-sample profiles were shaped by role (yds/catch, catches/game, frame). Alabama: Coleman-Williams is WR1 (d1).
//    Round 2: 406 WRs matched to PFF's 2026 team grade pages; for rows not hand-graded, the production traits (routes,
//    hands, awareness, release, YAC, body control) moved toward the PFF offense grade, mean-matched within P4 / G6 and
//    weighted by snaps (at most 4 points; Army/Navy/Air Force skipped, their WR grades are mostly blocking); 34 hand rows
//    nudged where PFF disagreed; 21 American/CUSA/Sun Belt speeds and hands set from 247 track times and evaluations.
// 7. Size is physical, from ESPN height/weight, on the NFL files' own size scales:
//    QB  size = -88.30 + 1.0211 x in + 0.08298 x lb (least-squares fit to qbs.js, mean error 0.2)
//    WR  75% height + 25% weight, 66 in / 155 lb = 0, 77 in / 231 lb = 11 (wrs.js)
//    RB  80% weight + 20% height, 178 lb / 67 in = 0, 247 lb / 75 in = 11 (rbs.js)
// ovr: the same formulas as utils/simulation.js (calcOVR, calcOVRWR, calcOVRRB).
//
// Trait recipes (z-scores; "-" = lower is better):
//  QB  arm: yds/completion .5, yds/att .3, longest pass .2
//      accuracy: completion % over expected for his depth (completion % vs yds/completion trend, a CPOE stand-in) .55, completion % .3, -INT % .15
//      legs: rushing yds/game with sack yards added back (college counts sacks as runs) .6, yds/carry on non-sack runs .25, rush TD/game .15 (no schedule bump)
//      processing (pre-snap): ESPN Total QBR .35, -INT % .25, -sack % .2, career attempts .2
//      vision (post-snap): TD % .3, -INT % .3, QBR .25, yds/att .15
//      playmaking: QBR .3, rushing yds/game .25, yds/att .2, TD % .15, rush TD/game .1
//      pocket-presence: -sack % (sacks / dropbacks) .55, passer rating .25, -INT % .2
//      leadership: career attempts .45, team record in his 2026 starts .35, QBR .2
//  WR  speed: share of catches 20+ yds .4, yds/catch .3, longest catch .15, YAC/catch .15
//      bodyControl: TD/catch .35, yds/catch .35, 1st downs/catch .3
//      vertical: yds/catch .35, TD/catch .3, height .35
//      routeRunning: share of team completions .45, 1st downs/catch .3, catches/game .25
//      release: share of team pass yds .5, share of team completions .3, yds/game .2
//      hands: share of team completions .5, 1st downs/catch .3, -fumbles/catch .2 (ESPN has no college targets or drops)
//      awareness: 1st downs/catch .35, TD/catch .25, career catches .4
//      afterCatch: YAC/catch .7, share of catches 20+ yds .3
//  RB  speed: share of games with a 20+ yd run .4, yds/carry .35, longest run .25
//      burst: yds/carry .45, 20+ run games .3, 1st downs/carry .25
//      strength: weight .4, TD/carry .3, 1st downs/carry .3
//      balance: yds/carry .45, 1st downs/carry .3, carries/game .25
//      elusiveness: 20+ run games .4, yds/carry .3, YAC/catch .3
//      vision: 1st downs/carry .4, yds/carry .35, carries/game .25
//      hands: catches/game .55, yds/catch .25, -fumbles/touch .2
//      carrying: ball security only, ESPN 2026 fumbles per touch shrunk toward 1 per 90 touches:
//        est = (fumbles + 1) / (touches + 80), grade = 5.6 + 1.6 x log2((1/90) / est), off the curve
//        (career fumble history overrides it for Baugh, Lacy and Isaac Brown)
// (2026-only inputs: YAC, first downs, 20+ catches; ESPN's 2025 college feed doesn't carry them.)
//
// ── Sources ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  ESPN 2026 box scores (site.api.espn.com .../college-football/summary), team schedules and rosters
//  ESPN season stats 2024-2026 (site.web.api.espn.com .../college-football/statistics/byathlete, incl. Total QBR, YAC, first downs)
//  ESPN athlete bios and career stats (sports.core.api.espn.com .../athletes/{id}, .../athletes/{id}/stats and /gamelog)
//  ESPN FPI 2026 (site.api.espn.com .../college-football/powerindex) for team strength and opponent adjustment
//  PFF college grades are not public, so the formula doesn't use them; the RB hand grades use PFF figures quoted in
//  public articles and search snippets. Nothing here is from Wikipedia.

